Material inside it that belongs to others keeps its own terms:
  - Photographs and documents released by the U.S. government (the Department of
    Justice under the Epstein Files Transparency Act; the FBI; the House Committee
    on Oversight and Government Reform; court exhibits in United States v. Maxwell):
    U.S. government works, public domain. Each is credited in the page.
  - Press photographs (NBC News, CNN, Dafydd Jones, The LIFE Picture Collection and
    others) belong to their owners and are credited where shown. Getty Images
    photographs are not shown; each is described and linked.
  - Wikimedia Commons photographs under Creative Commons licences keep those
    licences; each is credited in the page.
  - Buildings, streets and places: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0.
  - Manhattan building footprints: City of New York, NYC Open Data.
  - Terrain: USGS 3DEP lidar (Florida Peninsular 2018; Puerto Rico & U.S. Virgin
    Islands 2018 and 2024; Santa Fe County 2014), Copernicus GLO-30 (ESA), Terrarium
    elevation tiles (AWS Open Data). Coastlines and borders: Natural Earth.
  - Outlines traced from aerial imagery: Esri World Imagery Wayback (traced by eye;
    no imagery is included).
